T: Hashire Kotaro
T: 走れコウタロー
C: Kenkichi Ikeda, Nobuo Maeda (1970)
O: Japan
N: 1970 hit for the folk group Salty Sugar (ソルティー・シュガー); a comic song about a racehorse. Still in copyright (Nichion).
N: Original key G, as printed. Verse (8 bars), chorus (8), then the final chorus, whose "hashire hashire hashire hashire" bars double the speed of the opening figure.
N: The spoken race-commentary section (serifu) is omitted - it is chanted speech on repeated notes, not a melody. Lyrics omitted.
N: Melody and chords from the Zen-On melody score (number notation + chords), cross-checked bar for bar against the Timely Music harmonica score and the Jiyu-Gendaisha vocal/guitar edition; form and chords confirmed against the Zen-On guitar chord chart ("Original key=G, Capo=0"). Tempo is editorial.
